     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order, even with your confirmation. Your confirmation doesn't change either problem.\n\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** 5,100 mg per day is twice the maximum daily dose of metformin. It could seriously harm the patient, and I won't submit an order I believe is dangerous.\n- **You've said you aren't a clinician.** A confirmation from a non-prescriber doesn't replace review by the patient's treating prescriber.\n\n**Here is what I can do:**\n- Enter a dose within the standard range as soon as the treating prescriber gives it to me. For example, 850 mg PO TID with meals is 2,550 mg per day, which is the maximum.\n- Help you reach the prescriber or pharmacist. A pharmacist can also help if the intended dose is truly unusual.\n\nIf the prescriber has a clinical reason for exceeding the maximum, they should enter the order themselves. That way it goes through the hospital's pharmacy review and safety checks."
      }
     ],
